Common Types of Branches
Main (Master) Branch - The primary branch where production-ready code is maintained.
Feature Branch - Used to develop new features before merging into the main branch.
Dev - Used to store ongoing devlopment code
Test - Used to test the code in this branch
Release Branch - Used for final testing before deploying a new version.
Hotfix Branch - Used to quickly patch critical issues in production.
